aMagic shifts /cIlona Andrews. 1aNew York :bAce Books,c2015.  a1 sound file :bdigital  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aaudio file2rda  aeAudiobook2tlcgt  aGeneral2tlctarget0 aKate Daniels novels  aElectronic audio file.  aElectronic reproduction.bRockvillecGraphicAudiod2025nAvailable via World Wide Web.10aDaniels, Katec(Fictitious character)vFiction. 0aShapeshiftingvFiction.. 0aMagicvFiction. 0aAtlanta (Ga.)vFiction. 7aFantasy fiction.2gsafd 7aElectronic audio books.2local2 aOverDrive, Inc.,edistributor.40zClick here to accessuhttp://link.overdrive.com/?websiteID=200561&titleID=1136319103017cim a2200409 i erc0001274053TLC20241108220528.0m        h        cr una||||||||sz usnnnn|||ed241108s2025    nyunnnn o|||||||| n eng d  a9781250381323 (electronic audio bk.)  a(OCoLC)1483232643  aA9384968-C5AA-4F0F-B59E-05A862E13D47bOverDrive, Inc.nhttp://www.overdrive.com  aTLCcTLCdTLCerda00aPS3603.A3774bA78 202500a813/.6223/eng/202407291 aCaffall, Eiren,eauthor.10aAll the water in the world :ba novel /cEiren Caffall. 1aNew York :bSt. Martin's Press,c2025.  a1 sound file :bdigital  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aaudio file2rda  aeAudiobook2tlcgt  aGeneral2tlctarget  aElectronic audio file.0 aRead by Eunice Wong.  a"In the tradition of Station Eleven, a literary thriller set partly on the roof of New York's Museum of Natural History in a flooded future. All the Water in the World is told in the voice of a girl gifted with a deep feeling for water. In the years after the glaciers melt, Nonie, her older sister and her parents and their researcher friends have stayed behind in an almost deserted New York City, creating a settlement on the roof of the American Museum of Natural History. The rule: Take from the exhibits only in dire need. They hunt and grow their food in Central Park as they work to save the collections of human history and science. When a superstorm breaches the city's flood walls, Nonie and her family must escape north on the Hudson. They carry with them a book that holds their records of the lost collections. Racing on the swollen river towards what may be safety, they encounter communities that have adapted in very different and sometimes frightening ways to the new reality. But they are determined to find a way to make a new world that honors all they've saved. Inspired by the stories of the curators in Iraq and Leningrad who worked to protect their collections from war, All the Water in the World is both a meditation on what we save from collapse and an adventure story-with danger, storms, and a fight for survival. In the spirit of From the Mixed-Up Files of Mrs. Basil E. Frankweiler and Parable of the Sower, this wild journey offers the hope that what matters most - love and work, community and knowledge - will survive"--cProvided by publisher.  aElectronic reproduction.bNew YorkcMacmillan Audiod2025nAvailable via World Wide Web. 7aApocalyptic fiction.2lcgft 7aNovels.2lcgft 7aElectronic audio books.2local2 aOverDrive, Inc.,edistributor.40zClick here to accessuhttp://link.overdrive.com/?websiteID=200561&titleID=1074994702922cim a2200445 i erc0001275967TLC20241118220343.0m        h        cr una||||||||sz usnnnn|||ed241118t20252025nyunnnn o|||||||| n eng d  a9780593946459 (electronic audio bk.)  a(OCoLC)1483684029  aDCFD2DF3-B7DF-4052-B391-82644E4D7F04bOverDrive, Inc.nhttp://www.overdrive.com  aTLCcTLCdTLCerda00aPS3606.A685bF38 202500a813/.6223/eng/202310261 aFargo, Layne,eauthor.14aThe favorites :ba novel /cLayne Fargo. 1aNew York :bRandom House,c2025. 4c©2025  a1 sound file :bdigital  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aaudio file2rda  aeAudiobook2tlcgt  aGeneral2tlctarget  aElectronic audio file.0 aRead by Christine Lakin.  a"She might not have a famous name, funding, or her family's support, but Katarina Shaw has always known that she was destined to become an Olympic skater. When she meets Heath Rocha, a lonely kid stuck in the foster care system, their instant connection makes them a formidable duo on the ice. Clinging to skating-and each other-to escape their turbulent lives, Kat and Heath go from childhood sweethearts to champion ice dancers, captivating the world with their scorching chemistry, rebellious style, and rollercoaster relationship. Until a shocking incident at the Olympic Games brings their partnership to a sudden end. As the ten-year anniversary of their final skate approaches, an unauthorized documentary reignites the public obsession with Shaw and Rocha, claiming to uncover the "real story" through interviews with their closest friends and fiercest rivals. Kat wants nothing to do with the documentary. But she can't stand the thought of someone else defining her legacy either. So, after a decade of silence, she's telling her story: from the childhood tragedies that created her all-consuming bond with Heath to the clash of desires that tore them apart. Sensational rumors have haunted their every step for years, but the truth may be even more shocking than the headlines"--cProvided by publisher.  aElectronic reproduction.bNew YorkcBooks on Taped2025nAvailable via World Wide Web. 0aIce skatingvFiction.. 0aOlympicsvFiction. 7aNovels.2lcgft 7aElectronic audio books.2local2 aOverDrive, Inc.,edistributor.08iOnline version:aFargo, Layne.tFavoritesbFirst Edition.dNew York : Random House, 2025.z9780593732052w(DLC) 202305045340zClick here to accessuhttp://link.overdrive.com/?websiteID=200561&titleID=1075061801627cim a2200409 i erc0001271878TLC20241101221512.0m        h        cr una||||||||sz usnnnn|||ed241101t20252025nyunnnn o|||||||| n eng d  a9781250381316 (electronic audio bk.)  a321FBB4E-28CB-4D2B-9C21-19442C99799FbOverDrive, Inc.nhttp://www.overdrive.com  aTLCcTLCdTLCerda00aPS3613.A7746bK55 202500a813/.6223/eng/202404181 aMarshall, Kate Alice,eauthor.12aA killing cold /cKate Alice Marshall. 1aNew York :bFlatiron Books,c2025. 4c©2025  a1 sound file :bdigital  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aaudio file2rda  aeAudiobook2tlcgt  aGeneral2tlctarget  aElectronic audio file.0 aRead by Karissa Vacker.  a"A woman invited to her wealthy fiance's family retreat realizes they are hiding a terrible secret - and that she's been there before, by the author of What Lies in the Woods and No One Can Know"--cProvided by publisher.  aElectronic reproduction.bNew YorkcMacmillan Audiod2025nAvailable via World Wide Web. 1aSecretsvFiction.. 7aNovels.2lcgft 7aElectronic audio books.2local2 aOverDrive, Inc.,edistributor.40zClick here to accessuhttp://link.overdrive.com/?websiteID=200561&titleID=1074994303085cim a2200409 i erc0001284681TLC20241230221740.0m        h        cr una||||||||sz usnnnn|||ed241230s2025    nyunnnn o|||||||| n eng d  a9781250383907 (electronic audio bk.)  a7BD20230-FA76-4FF4-B3FD-3F0EB122AA5FbOverDrive, Inc.nhttp://www.overdrive.com  aTLCcTLCdTLCerda00aHQ18.55b.B69 202500a305.3223/eng/202407301 aBoylan, Jennifer Finney,d1958-eauthor.10aCleavage :bmen, women, and the space between us /cJennifer Finney Boylan. 1aNew York :bCeladon Books,c2025.  a1 sound file :bdigital  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aaudio file2rda  aeAudiobook2tlcgt  aGeneral2tlctarget  aElectronic audio file.0 aRead by Gabra Zackman.  a"What is the difference between men and women? Jennifer Finney Boylan, bestselling author of She's Not There and co-author of Mad Honey with Jodi Picoult, examines the divisions-as well as the common ground-between the genders, and reflects on her own experiences, both difficult and joyful, as a transgender American. Jennifer Finney Boylan's She's Not There was the first bestselling work written by a transgender American. Since its publication twenty years ago, she has become the go-to person for insight into the impact of gender on our lives, from the food we eat to the dreams we dream, both for ourselves and for our children. But Cleavage is more than a deep dive into gender identity; it's also a look at the difference between coming out as trans in 2000-when many people reacted to Boylan's transition with love-and the present era of blowback and fear. How does gender affect our sense of self? Our body image? The passage of time? The friends we lose-and keep? Boylan considers her womanhood, reflects on the boys and men who shaped her, and reconceives of herself as a writer, activist, parent, and spouse. With heart-wrenching honesty, she illustrates the feeling of liminality that followed her to adulthood, but demonstrates the redemptive power of love through it all. With Boylan's trademark humor and poignancy, Cleavage is a sharp, witty, and captivating look at the triumphs and losses of a life lived in two genders. Cleavage provides hope for a future in which we all have the freedom to live joyfully as men, as women, and in the space between us"--cProvided by publisher.  aElectronic reproduction.bNew YorkcMacmillan Audiod2025nAvailable via World Wide Web.10aBoylan, Jennifer Finney,d1958- 0aGender identity.. 0aTransgender peoplexIdentity. 7aElectronic audio books.2local2 aOverDrive, Inc.,edistributor.40zClick here to accessuhttp://link.overdrive.com/?websiteID=200561&titleID=1069991801567cim a2200409 i erc0001291158TLC20250121225150.0m        h        cr una||||||||sz usnnnn|||ed250121t20252024nyunnnn o|||||||| n eng d  a9781250419026 (electronic audio bk.)  a(OCoLC)1485592808  aE461AE99-2CF7-